#N canvas 40 60 1280 1010 12;
#X declare -path ..;
#X obj 0 0 cnv 1 1280 46 empty empty 15\ \ \ Diffusion\ \ -\ \ denoising\ a\ noise\ cloud\ into\ a\ chord\ (2015\ /\ 2020) 14 23 0 20 #1d3557 #ffffff 0;
#X obj 1110 980 declare -path ..;
#X text 800 980 finds the nn.* objects one folder up ->, f 42;
#X text 20 980 neuralplay - Moisés Horta Valenzuela / SEMILLA.AI Studio, f 70;
#X text 20 56 Image and audio generators like Stable Diffusion and Stable Audio start from pure NOISE and remove a little of it \, step by step \, until a picture or a sound appears. Here six voices start as a random cloud of pitches and are "denoised" into a chord. Listen to the harmony condense out of the noise., f 175;
#X obj 10 96 cnv 1 390 890 empty empty THE\ IDEA 8 12 0 13 #eef1f5 #1d3557 0;
#X text 20 122 DIFFUSION MODELS (Sohl-Dickstein et al. 2015 \, Song and Ermon 2019 \, Ho et al. 2020) learn the reverse of a slow destruction: take real data \, add more and more noise until nothing is left - then train a network to undo one small step of that \, at every noise level., f 52;
#X text 20 218 To GENERATE: start from pure noise and apply the denoiser again and again \, with less noise each time. What the network has learned is the SCORE: at every point \, which direction leads towards more likely data., f 52;
#X text 20 299 HERE the "data" is a chord: pitches that sit on chord tones are likely. Its score can be written down exactly (open [pd one-denoising-step]) \, so no training is needed - but the sampling loop is the real one (annealed Langevin dynamics):, f 52;
#X text 30 395 x = x + eps * score(x \, sigma) + sqrt(2 eps) * noise, f 52;
#X text 20 431 Big sigma at the start: the score only knows "go towards the middle of the chord region" \, and the noise is large. Small sigma at the end: every voice is pulled onto its nearest chord tone. A last Tweedie step removes the remaining noise., f 52;
#X text 20 527 SOUND: DiffWave and WaveGrad (2020) generate waveforms this way \, Riffusion (2022) spectrogram images \, Stable Audio (2023) music. They all repeat this loop with a big neural network in place of our formula., f 52;
#X text 20 608 TRY: fewer steps (rushed: voices end off-key or on the same note) \, a bigger sigma_max (more chaos first) \, a smaller eta (too timid to arrive). Change the chord preset and denoise again., f 52;
#X obj 410 96 cnv 1 860 470 empty empty TRAJECTORIES:\ pitch\ (MIDI\ 36\ ..\ 90)\ of\ the\ 6\ voices\ over\ the\ denoising\ steps 8 12 0 13 #e3f0fb #1d3557 0;
