#X text 20 10 ONE DENOISING STEP (the trigger fires right to left: 1 -> 3). For every voice x: score = (sum_k w_k (mu_k - x) / v) / (sum_k w_k) \, with w_k = exp(-(mu_k - x)^2 / (2 v)) and v = 0.2^2 + sigma^2. That is the slope of log p(x) for a distribution made of soft bumps at the chord tones mu_k \, blurred by the current noise level sigma. Langevin: x = x + eps * score + sqrt(2 eps) * noise \, with eps = eta * sigma^2., f 170;
#X obj 20 100 inlet;
#X obj 20 126 t b b b;
#X text 700 170 1) this step's noise level: sigma shrinks geometrically from sigma_max to sigma_min. eps = step size \, v = blurred variance. In the final step (fin = 1) sigma = sigma_min., f 70;
#X obj 60 170 expr if(fin_\$0 \, smin_\$0 \, smax_\$0 * pow(smin_\$0 / smax_\$0 \, t_\$0 / max(T_\$0 - 1 \, 1))), f 60;
#X obj 60 210 t f f f;
#X obj 500 240 v sig_\$0;
#X obj 260 240 expr eta_\$0 * \$f1 * \$f1;
#X obj 260 266 v eps_\$0;
#X obj 60 240 expr 0.04 + \$f1 * \$f1;
#X obj 60 266 v v_\$0;
#X text 700 320 2) for every voice i: read x \, reset the sums \, let every chord tone pull (num) and weigh in (den) \, then move x. The final step uses Tweedie's formula instead: jump to the expected clean pitch \, x + v * score (no noise)., f 70;
#X obj 60 320 t b;
#X obj 60 346 t b b;
#X msg 120 372 0;
#X msg 60 372 6;
#X obj 60 398 until;
#X obj 60 424 f;
#X obj 110 424 + 1;
#X obj 60 456 t b b b f;
#X obj 420 486 v i_\$0;
#X obj 500 486 expr xv\$0[\$f1];
#X obj 500 512 v xi_\$0;
#X msg 300 486 0 0;
#X obj 300 512 unpack f f;
#X obj 300 538 v num_\$0;
#X obj 380 538 v den_\$0;
#X obj 140 576 t b;
#X obj 140 602 t b b;
#X msg 200 628 0;
#X obj 140 628 v K_\$0;
#X obj 140 654 until;
#X obj 140 680 f;
#X obj 190 680 + 1;
#X obj 140 712 expr num_\$0 + exp(-(ch\$0[\$f1] - xi_\$0) * (ch\$0[\$f1] - xi_\$0) / (2 * v_\$0)) * (ch\$0[\$f1] - xi_\$0) / v_\$0 \; den_\$0 + exp(-(ch\$0[\$f1] - xi_\$0) * (ch\$0[\$f1] - xi_\$0) / (2 * v_\$0)), f 70;
#X obj 140 800 v num_\$0;
#X obj 260 800 v den_\$0;
#X text 600 712 <- one chord tone k pulls voice i (^ would be XOR in [expr] \, so squares are written as products), f 30;
#X obj 60 850 expr xv\$0[i_\$0] = xi_\$0 + if(fin_\$0 \, v_\$0 * num_\$0 / max(den_\$0 \, 1e-30) \, eps_\$0 * num_\$0 / max(den_\$0 \, 1e-30) + sqrt(2 * eps_\$0) * sqrt(-2 * log((float(random(0 \, 32767)) + 1) / 32768)) * cos(6.283185 * float(random(0 \, 32767)) / 32768)), f 80;
#X text 700 930 3) write the new pitches into the trajectory plot (index = step scaled to 300 points) and send them to the voices., f 70;
#X obj 20 930 t b b;
#X obj 160 956 expr int(t_\$0 * 299 / max(T_\$0 - 1 \, 1));
#X obj 160 990 t f f f f f f;
#X obj 20 1030 expr min(max(xv\$0[0] \, 36) \, 90) \; min(max(xv\$0[1] \, 36) \, 90) \; min(max(xv\$0[2] \, 36) \, 90) \; min(max(xv\$0[3] \, 36) \, 90) \; min(max(xv\$0[4] \, 36) \, 90) \; min(max(xv\$0[5] \, 36) \, 90), f 90;
